  "published": "2026-06-02T01:58:35.967Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.0.0-preview.1: Maturity-tier bump from 0.3.0-preview.1. No new algorithm suite, no algorithm agility — the crypto core (ML-DSA-65 signatures, X-Wing + AES-256-GCM optional encryption, sign-then-encrypt, RFC 7516 AAD binding, fail-closed validation) is unchanged. The 1.0 tier brings a sharper safety posture: a RequireReplayProtection flag so an operator can't forget to wire a replay cache (silent OFF case now opt-in fail-closed), an internal test seam (IXWingDeterministicCoins) that lets the suite KAT the X-Wing combiner and the X25519 ephemeral half against deterministic inputs (the BCL ML-KEM encapsulation path still cannot be KAT'd — that gap is narrowed and re-documented in KNOWN-GAPS.md), a 64-iteration statistical sanity test on encapsulation, a pinned end-to-end roundtrip corpus, and a \"Read this first\" README disclosure that these tokens use non-IANA-registered identifiers and will NOT validate in generic JWT tooling. Includes the previously-unreleased PqJwtValidationException wrapping fix. The preview.N suffix continues to carry the maturity caveat: NOT independently audited, NOT for production. Full notes: https://github.com/systemslibrarian/postquantum-jwt/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md — known limitations: https://github.com/systemslibrarian/postquantum-jwt/blob/main/KNOWN-GAPS.md.",
